# Options the spec does not have: ours is a usage error; macOS accepts them.
-f "$(id -u)" f
-n "$(id -u)" f
-Rx "$(id -u)" f
-v "$(id -u)" f
-x "$(id -u)" f
# A dangling link (an operand, or met in a tree) that chown would follow: ours and GNU report the missing target; macOS changes the link itself and succeeds.
